{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מה טבו אהליך", :translit "mah tovu ohalekha", :gloss "How goodly are your tents"} {:he "ששה תיבות בפסוק", :translit "shishah teivot ba-pasuk", :gloss "Six words in the verse"} {:he "ששה אהלים", :translit "shishah ohalim", :gloss "six tents"} {:he "נוב וגבעון גלגל שילה ובית עולמים שנים", :translit "nov ve-giv'on gilgal shiloh u-veit olamim shnayim", :gloss "Nov and Givon, Gilgal, Shiloh, and the Eternal House — two"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Six words in the verse correspond to six sanctuaries: Nov, Givon, Gilgal, Shiloh, and the two of the Eternal House (first and second Temples)."}], :frame {:text "The places where the Tabernacle and Temple stood are enumerated in rabbinic tradition as Nov, Givon, Gilgal, Shiloh, and the Eternal House (Beit Olamim) in Jerusalem (Zevachim 14b–16b, sometimes listed as seven or as a fixed sequence). The phrase 'Beit Olamim' as the Temple's name derives from 1 Kings 8:13. Jacob's association with the concept of 'tent' draws on Genesis 25:27, where he is called 'a dweller in tents.'", :sources ["Zevachim 14b" "Zevachim 16b" "Genesis 25:27" "1 Kings 8:13"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Six words in the verse correspond to six sanctuaries: Nov, Givon, Gilgal, Shiloh, and the two of the Eternal House (first and second Temples).", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:31:07.107305446Z", :model "glm-5.2"}